course: dictionary
lesson: 8060
title: Rejection and the feelings behind it
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Rejection is a word for saying no, or for being turned down. A shop can reject a faulty toy and send it back. The word comes from reject, which means to refuse or not accept.
explain: Read «Most actors are not famous; many do small roles, adverts and voice work, and face many auditions and rejections.» The clues are auditions, where actors try out for parts, and not famous. Actors try out, and often they are not chosen, so rejections must mean times they were turned down.
explain: Rejection can also be a feeling, like being left out. When you are not picked for a team or not invited to a party, that hurt is rejection. When you meet the word, ask: is someone saying no, or is someone being left out?
fact: «Rejection» means refusing to accept something, or the feeling of not being chosen.
fact: «Rejections» is the plural: many times someone has said no.
fact: In medicine, rejection is when the body attacks a new organ after a transplant.
fact: Authors and inventors often face many rejections before they succeed.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «Most actors ... face many auditions and rejections.» What does rejections mean here? | *Times when actors were turned down | Costumes for the stage | Times when actors were given a big prize | Happy days on set
exercise: Ben's painting was turned down by the gallery. What is this called? | Performance | Transplant | Audition | *Rejection
exercise: Doctors give medicine because the body may show rejection after a transplant. Where does the rejection happen? | In the hospital car park | In the sky | In a school playground | *In the body, when it attacks a new organ
test: Why do authors and inventors face many rejections? | Because they are always famous | *Because their work is often turned down before it succeeds | Because they never write anything | Because rejection is a kind of prize
test: Lena was not picked for the team. Which word describes the hurt she feels? | Famished | Drooped | *Rejection | Curt
exam: Which situation shows rejection as a feeling? | *Mia was left out of the party and felt unwanted | The garden was full of bright flowers | The bus was late this morning | The gallery sent back a faulty vase
